Ouch, ouch, ouch.  RN God got you.

The only thing I can think of is that you didn't keep track of the
Three.  If you had telepathy and a towel/blindfold - very usual in an
ascendable character - you should generally put on the towel and check
out where the Three are as soon you get into astral - i.e. *before*
fighting any monsters that happen to be hanging around.  The usual
thing to do is, after summoning pets, either stuff yourself satiated
and kill Famine, or bring out your full healings and kill Pestilence.

Also, it's the usual reason why some prefer to keep a light source
handy - either a magic lamp if you could find and spare one or a bunch
of lamps (refilling one with oil is less convenient - particularly if
oil is scarce - than just dumping it and going to the next).  Not to
mention the inherent advantages of, say, Knights with lances or
Rangers and Rogues with ranged attacks get from being able to see
further.

